) Thought: I have already opened the settings panel in VS Code and searched for \"tab\", and now I can see the settings related to tabs. I need to locate the \"Editor: Tab Size\" option to configure tab wrapping. I should click on \"Editor: Tab Size\" and change its value to a larger number, which will enable automatic tab wrapping when the tabs exceed the available space. Action: click(start_box='(520,406)') Thought: I have successfully opened the settings panel in VS Code and located the \"Editor: Tab Size\" option. Now, I need to change the current value from 4 to 8 to enable tab wrapping. I should first delete the current value 4, then enter the new value 8. To do this, I should press Ctrl+A to select all the text, and then type the new value 8. Action: hotkey(key='ctrl a') Thought: I have selected the current value 4 of \"Editor: Tab Size\" and now need to enter the new value 8 to enable tab wrapping. I should simply type 8 to replace the selected value 4.。 Action: type(content='8') Thought: I have successfully changed the value of \"Editor: Tab Size\" from 4 to 8, and now I need to save this setting. In VS Code, I can use the shortcut Ctrl+S to save the settings. I should use the shortcut Ctrl+S to save the changes made to the tab wrapping settings in VS Code. Action: hotkey(key='ctrl s') 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8Our Model Thought: I have opened the Insert menu and now need to click the \"Image...\" option to insert an image. This option is located at the top of the menu. I should click the \"Image...\" option under the Insert menu to open the file selection dialog and choose the image to insert. Action: click(start_box='(132,71)') Thought: I need to add a 1cm by 1cm image to slide 2. From the current interface, I can see that I first need to click the slide thumbnail on the left to select slide 2. I should first click the thumbnail of the second slide in the left slide panel to begin editing. Action: click(start_box='(86,358)') Thought: I have successfully selected sli